JAM 4, Aug 3, 2026, 13:37 GMT+2

Hi,

Thanks for your email and interest in Loudly!

While Loudly-generated music may be used commercially in accordance with =
the applicable subscription license, the standard Loudly license does not=
 permit the generated tracks to be included in a commercial music library=
 or licensed onward to third-party business customers as standalone music=
 content.

This means that the proposed CMLP model=E2=80=94where Loudly-generated tr=
acks would form part of your catalogue and be licensed to hotels, retail =
businesses, offices, gyms, or other customers for public playback=E2=80=94=
is not permitted under the standard subscription license.

The commercial license is intended to allow you to use the music within y=
our own projects and productions. It does not grant the right to resell, =
sublicense, redistribute, or make the music available as a standalone cat=
alogue or stock/library music service.

Regarding ownership and duration, your rights to use music generated and =
downloaded under an active qualifying subscription remain subject to the =
applicable Loudly License Agreement. However, the standard license does n=
ot provide exclusive ownership of the generated output.

Regarding collecting-society royalties and public-performance obligations=
, Loudly does not provide legal or collecting-society advice. Any applica=
ble licensing or royalty requirements may depend on the country, the spec=
ific use, and the relevant collecting society. We recommend consulting th=
e relevant organization or a qualified legal professional for guidance.

If you have any further inquiries, please do not hesitate to contact us.

Best regards,

* * *

Your Loudly Team

**Music Maker JAM**
**Loudly**

